  "prompt_text": "REQUEST_ID clubs-corners-batch02-20261026. Reference 1 is a simple geometry diagram, not final art: copy its exact cell order and principal silhouette logic. Reference 2 is a verified approved same-kit orthographic wall-view guide; use it to transfer realistic camera and structural detail. Reference 3 is the canonical material/identity contact for two target corner assets, outer row then inner row; it alone controls black/red panel identity, gold trim, and finish. Create a transparent pixel-art atlas with TWO rows and SIX equal columns ordered FRONT, TOP, RIGHT, LEFT, BOTTOM, REAR. For each row, the four horizontal views (FRONT, RIGHT, LEFT, REAR) MUST be broad, level, axis-aligned rectangular elevations of the joined corner assembly, equal total height and consistent broad face proportions. Never use an isometric corner silhouette in these four columns; no visible top planes; never a skinny single post. The TOP and BOTTOM cells MUST show a clear L-shaped footprint: a central square corner block, one short rectangular arm extending right and one short rectangular arm extending down, leaving one quadrant empty. Both plan cells have this same outer L outline. Keep exactly one short wall panel per arm, no three-panel-long wall. Repaint in row-specific target design: outer uses dark black inset panel faces with gold edge; inner uses red illuminated wood panel faces with gold edge; both have heavy black framing and square gold-trim corner block. In all views, preserve the square corner block and joined two-wing construction. Hidden faces are conservative inferred extensions of target materials. Pure orthographic, no perspective, no isometric, no objects, labels, floor, cast shadow, or cell overlap. Pixel art, crisp edges, transparent background."
